      "Language": "hun",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The case history of a 71-year-old woman with acute dyspnoea caused by a giant leiomyoma and severe acute anemia due to intratumoral hemorrhage is presented. Urgent operation was performed, and a 13.5 kg pendular tumor was removed. The cornerstones of the differential diagnoses and therapy of giant abdominal tumors is discussed."},
